1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,615
You always see lightning first

2
00:00:01,615 --> 00:00:02,726
then the thunder rolls in!

3
00:00:02,726 --> 00:00:03,206
Why?

4
00:00:03,406 --> 00:00:04,777
Both happen at the same instant

5
00:00:04,777 --> 00:00:06,095
but they travel to you differently

6
00:00:06,095 --> 00:00:07,764
Light is way faster than sound

7
00:00:07,964 --> 00:00:09,514
Light crosses the gap instantly

8
00:00:09,514 --> 00:00:10,780
Sound just strolls along

9
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:12,835
about 1 km every 3 seconds

10
00:00:12,835 --> 00:00:14,300
so the thunder arrives late

11
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,410
Here's a handy trick

12
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:16,962
Count the seconds after the flash

13
00:00:16,962 --> 00:00:17,884
divide by three

14
00:00:17,884 --> 00:00:19,353
and you get the storm's distance

15
00:00:19,553 --> 00:00:22,108
9 seconds? About 3 km away

16
00:00:22,108 --> 00:00:23,797
Shorter gap, closer storm

17
00:00:23,997 --> 00:00:25,501
That's why you see lightning first!
